# Quant AGI frontend deploy

After changing `quant_agi/frontend`, **always rebuild and restart** the PM2 process before expecting `/quant-agi-terminal` to work on production.

## Required command

```bash
cd quant_agi/frontend && npm run build:deploy
```

Equivalent manual steps:

```bash
cd quant_agi/frontend && npm run build && pm2 restart quant-agi-frontend --update-env
```

## Why

Next.js `next start` loads the build manifest at process start. Running `npm run build` without restarting PM2 leaves a stale manifest — page chunks like `/_next/static/chunks/app/page-*.js` return **404** and the terminal shows:

> Application error: a client-side exception has occurred

## When to apply

- After any Quant AGI frontend code change you want live on `app.keepitbased.com`
- After `npm run build` in `quant_agi/frontend` (even if deploy script was not used)
- `scripts/deploy-production.sh` already restarts `quant-agi-frontend`; ad-hoc builds must too
